# openOODA x86 Post-Fix Static Projection

Logline: Projects the post-fix silent-miscompile rate and SSA ASM-FAIL rate from the v2 hostile-probe numbers plus static analysis of the four landed fixes, without re-running the 3-hour probe.

Setup: Reads audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot (167 lines, pre-fix ground truth), audit/simd-deep.oot (142 lines, Float deep audit), audit/x86-runtime-blob-tail.oot (176 lines, no-op main analysis), and audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot (40 lines, SSA static projection). Four fixes have landed since v2: 5-shape refuse gate at the dispatcher, per-arm `wrote == 0` counter for struct / list / opt / free / typed_let / match, SSA per-block remap fix, and SIMD Float fold fix (sci-notation, 0/0, -0.0). No probe was re-run.

Beats:
  1. Recap the pre-fix numbers and the dominant root causes.
  2. Project the post-fix per-shape empty-stdout rate for the 5 hostile shapes.
  3. Project the post-fix SSA ASM-FAIL rate.
  4. Combine the per-shape and SSA projections into the final rates.
  5. State the confidence level and what would raise it.

File: openOODA/audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot
THIS FILE IS GENERATED — DO NOT EDIT. Source: x86 post-fix static projection 2026-08-25.

