## 1. Pre-fix numbers (from x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot)

The v2 probe ran on the same 6,936-fixture set that this projection targets. Key numbers, copy-pasted from v2 §2-§5:

| Metric                                    | Count  | % of base |
|-------------------------------------------|--------|-----------|
| COMPILED (emit-x86)                       |  5,750 |   82.9% of 6,936 |
| REFUSED (emit-x86)                        |  1,185 |   17.1% of 6,936 |
| ASM-FAIL (emit-x86)                       |      1 |    0.0% of 6,936 |
| Silent miscompile (empty stdout)          |  2,607 |   45.3% of 5,750 COMPILED |
| Of which no-op main (probe §4)            |  2,595 |   99.5% of 2,607 |
| SSA COMPILED (emit-x86-ssa)               |    508 |    7.3% of 6,936 |
| SSA REFUSED                               |      2 |    0.0% of 6,936 |
| SSA ASM-FAIL                              |  6,426 |   92.6% of 6,936 |
| SSA ASM-FAIL: duplicate label root cause  |  3,215 |   46.4% of 6,936 |
| SSA ASM-FAIL: undefined block ref cause   |  3,211 |   46.3% of 6,936 |

The 2,607 empty-stdout binaries decompose as 580 that have at least one of the 5 hostile shapes (struct, List, Result, Float, 3-arm match), 80 that are pure arithmetic / println / let, and ~1,947 that are explained by the loose matchers in the dedicated arms (any `IDENT.IDENT` matches `x86_match_struct`, any unmatched println chain can fall through to a no-op arm).

The 5 hostile shapes, with pre-fix empty / total-with-feature:

| # | Shape        | empty / total | rate  |
|---|--------------|---------------|-------|
| 1 | Float        | 158 / 160     | 98.7% |
| 2 | 3-arm match  |  27 /  30     | 90.0% |
| 3 | Result[T]    | 179 / 216     | 82.8% |
| 4 | struct       | 224 / 277     | 80.8% |
| 5 | List[T]      | 162 / 202     | 80.1% |

These five shapes overlap heavily in the fixture set (a program that uses Result almost always uses List or struct), so the union is much smaller than the sum. The probe estimated the union at ~580 of 2,607.

