## 2. Per-shape post-fix estimate

For each of the 5 hostile shapes, the post-fix rate is the empty-stdout rate (the % of COMPILED binaries that produce no stdout) for binaries that use the shape, after the four landed fixes.

The 5-shape refuse gate refuses Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, and List[T] at the dispatcher (x86_emit.oo:46-195). The per-arm `wrote == 0` counter is a defense-in-depth check on struct, list, opt, free, typed_let, and match arms (x86-runtime-blob-tail.oot §6.1). The SIMD Float fix (simd-deep.oot §1, gaps #1-#5) makes the Float const-fold handle sci-notation, 0/0, and -0.0 correctly, so Float programs that do reach the const-fold will produce a correct println instead of folding to 0.

| # | Shape        | Pre-fix empty-stdout | Post-fix estimate | Reasoning |
|---|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|-----------|
| 1 | Float        | 158 / 160 = 98.7%    | ~0 / ~160 = ~0%   | 5-shape refuse gate refuses Float at the dispatch before emission. The 158 silent-miscompile binaries all become REFUSED. The 2 that did not miscompile (e.g. 0/0 fold to 0.0, or no-println sources) are also refused. SIMD fix reduces residual risk for any Float path that bypasses the gate. |
| 2 | 3-arm match  |  27 /  30 = 90.0%    | ~0 /  ~30 = ~0%   | 5-shape refuse gate refuses 3-arm match at the dispatch. All 30 binaries become REFUSED. Per-arm `wrote == 0` counter on the match arm catches any non-3-arm match that bypasses the gate. |
| 3 | Result[T]    | 179 / 216 = 82.8%    | ~0 / ~216 = ~0%   | 5-shape refuse gate refuses Result[T] at the dispatch. All 216 binaries become REFUSED. Result was a result-shape identifier that the 22-arm chain had no real emitter for, so refusal is the right answer. |
| 4 | struct       | 224 / 277 = 80.8%    | ~0 / ~277 = ~0%   | 5-shape refuse gate refuses struct at the dispatch. All 277 binaries become REFUSED. Per-arm `wrote == 0` counter on x86_emit_struct is defense-in-depth for any struct path that bypasses the gate. The 224 silent-miscompile cases all become REFUSED. |
| 5 | List[T]      | 162 / 202 = 80.1%    | ~0 / ~202 = ~0%   | 5-shape refuse gate refuses List[T] at the dispatch. All 202 binaries become REFUSED. Per-arm `wrote == 0` counter on x86_emit_list is defense-in-depth. The 162 silent-miscompile cases all become REFUSED. |

Row count: 5 (one per hostile shape, matches acceptance criterion).

Side effect on the other empty-stdout sources: the per-arm `wrote == 0` counter on the 6 dedicated arms converts the dominant root cause (no-op main in struct, list, opt, free, typed_let, match) into REFUSED. The x86-runtime-blob-tail.oot §6.4 projection says COMPILED with empty stdout drops from 2,607 to ~12 after the per-arm wrote counter alone. The 12 remaining are the binaries that have a real write syscall but the syscall writes the wrong string (probe §10 caveat).

