## 3. SSA post-fix estimate

The SSA per-block remap fix in x86_ssa_emit.oo targets both root causes identified in v2 §3 (x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot §2). The fix:
- Suffixes the four `.Lxss_pi_*` labels with `inst_id.to_string()` to make them unique per instruction (line 101).
- Emits one `.L<fn_name>_<bname>:` label per block via `x86_ssa_emit_function` (line 44), so the forward reference from opcodes 17 (jmp) and 18 (cond_br) resolves.

| # | SSA root cause                        | Pre-fix ASM-FAIL | Post-fix estimate | Reasoning |
|---|---------------------------------------|------------------|-------------------|-----------|
| 1 | Duplicate `.Lxss_pi_*` labels         |  3,215 (46.4%)   |  ~0               | Per-instruction suffix makes labels unique; `as` accepts. Hard-coded "match" suffix at line 240 is in a different code path, no collision. |
| 2 | Undefined `.Lmain_block*` references  |  3,211 (46.3%)   |  ~0               | block_names now contains every block; emit_function emits one label per block; `ld` accepts. `as` allows forward references. |
| 3 | Residual: v1 14-fixture `movq` bug    |    14 (0.2%)     |  0-14 (0.0-0.2%)  | x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot §3.1 notes the v1 64-bit operand widening may or may not have landed. If it did, 0; if not, the 14 v1 fixtures re-surface. |
| 4 | Residual: block name collision        |      0           |  0-7 (0.0-0.1%)   | x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot §3.3. Remap is expected to produce unique bnames; smoke would catch a regression. |
|   | **New SSA ASM-FAIL total**            |  **6,426 (92.6%)**| **0-21 (0.0-0.3%)** | Sum of residual risks 3 and 4. |

The pre-fix COMPILED 508 (7.3%) stay COMPILED. The 2 REFUSED stay REFUSED. The 6,426 ASM-FAIL split: 6,405-6,426 move to COMPILED (depending on the v1 operand bug), 0-21 remain ASM-FAIL.

Post-fix SSA COMPILED: 508 + (6,426 - residual) = 6,913-6,934 of 6,936. New SSA ASM-FAIL rate: 0.0-0.3%, central estimate 0.05% (3/6,936).

