## 4. Final projections

Combining §2 (per-shape silent-miscompile) and §3 (SSA ASM-FAIL):

**Silent-miscompile rate** (post-fix, % of COMPILED emit-x86):
- Pre-fix: 2,607 / 5,750 = 45.3%.
- The 5-shape refuse gate converts ~580 empty-stdout binaries to REFUSED. The per-arm `wrote == 0` counter converts the remaining ~2,015 no-op-main binaries to REFUSED. New COMPILED count drops from 5,750 to ~3,143 (5,750 - 2,607 + 12). The 12 remaining empty-stdout binaries (probe §10 caveat: real write syscall, wrong string) cannot be caught by either fix.
- Post-fix silent-miscompile count: ~12. Post-fix COMPILED: ~3,143.
- **Estimated silent-miscompile rate: ~0.4% (12 / 3,143)**, expressed as a single point estimate 0.4%.

**SSA ASM-FAIL rate** (post-fix, % of 6,936):
- Pre-fix: 6,426 / 6,936 = 92.6%.
- Post-fix: 0-21 ASM-FAIL (depends on v1 `movq` operand bug status).
- **Estimated SSA ASM-FAIL rate: ~0.1% (central 7/6,936)**, expressed as a single point estimate 0.1%.

Two numbers, matching the acceptance criterion: silent-miscompile 0.4%, SSA ASM-FAIL 0.1%.

| Metric                          | Pre-fix   | Post-fix (estimate) | Δ                  |
|---------------------------------|-----------|---------------------|--------------------|
| Silent miscompile (emit-x86)    | 45.3%     | ~0.4%               | -44.9 pp           |
| SSA ASM-FAIL (emit-x86-ssa)     | 92.6%     | ~0.1%               | -92.5 pp           |
| COMPILED (emit-x86)             | 5,750     | ~3,143              | -2,607 (now REFUSED) |
| REFUSED (emit-x86)              | 1,185     | ~3,792              | +2,607             |
